{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795433113,"nonce":"65gR6ccapTJWPWA4iWCf9sZnGn4=","title":"cn_demo passes pixel spacing tokens to the 4 px unit setters","message":"`cn_demo.rs` builds most of its spacing as `.p(theme.spacing().space_3)`, `.gap(theme.spacing().space_8)`, `.gap(12.0)`, `.gap(16.0)` and so on. The theme's spacing tokens are pixels (`space_3` is 12 px with the default base), and `Div::p`, `px`, `gap` take 4 px units, so every such value is drawn four times its size: 48 px page padding, 128 px between sections, 48 px between buttons, 64 px between a progress bar and its label. It shows as the very large gaps in the page (between a section title and its content, between buttons).\n\nThe narrow-window fix kept these as they are at desktop width, apart from the sidebar inset, whose 96 px padding broke its text, now `p_px(24.0)`, and a narrower page padding below 640 px.\n\nFix: use the `_px` setters (`p_px`, `gap_px`) for token and pixel values throughout the demo, then compare the page against the current one section by section with `cn_demo_widths` (`WIDTHS_SNAP`, `WIDTHS_SECTION`), since every section's spacing changes.","files":null}]}